      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s hierarchical, would it list all the projects under the hierarchy?\n\nEven if it\u0027s not, I think it should be possible for a user to use a project-scoped token to list their own, single, project. For example, I\u0027ve been frustrated trying to use osc with the trusts API because if you provide a username and project name rather than IDs, osc uses the list_projects and list_users commands to try to find the IDs of these resources. If you\u0027re not the admin user, it fails because regular users aren\u0027t allowed to list_projects or list_users, so you\u0027re forced to use IDs. If regular users could use a project-scoped token to list projects relevant to that project, even if it\u0027s just one project, that would help a lot.",
